: #fff;font-size: 11px;font-family: Verdana, Geneva, DejaVu Sans,sans-serif;\"><span style=\"padding:4px 4px 4px 6px;background: #555;border-top-left-radius: 4px;border-bottom-left-radius: 4px;\">stars</span><span style=\"padding: 4px 6px 4px 4px;background: #007ec6;border-top-right-radius: 4px;border-bottom-right-radius: 4px;\">1.8k</span></span></a><!--TRACK_AWESOME_REPO_ITEM_START____{\"type\":\"repo\",\"stargazerCount\":1807,\"repo\":\"ttt30ga/awesome-product-design\"}____TRACK_AWESOME_REPO_ITEM_END--> - Design a product from the initial concept to production.</li>","updatedAt":"2022-02-14T15:44:27.000Z"},{"awesomeListRepo":"sindresorhus/awesome","categoryHTML":"<h2>Miscellaneous</h2>","itemHTML":"<li><a href=\"https://github.com/make-github-pseudonymous-again/awesome-qr-code#readme\">QR Code</a><a data-role=\"trackawesomelist-badge\" href=\"https://github.com/make-github-pseudonymous-again/awesome-qr-code#readme\" style=\"text-decoration:none;top: -2px;position: relative;margin-left:4px;margin-right:4px;font-weight:400;\"><span style=\"color: #fff;font-size: 11px;font-family: Verdana, Geneva, DejaVu Sans,sans-serif;\"><span style=\"padding:4px 4px 4px 6px;background: #555;border-top-left-radius: 4px;border-bottom-left-radius: 4px;\">stars</span><span style=\"padding: 4px 6px 4px 4px;background: #007ec6;border-top-right-radius: 4px;border-bottom-right-radius: 4px;\">39</span></span></a><!--TRACK_AWESOME_REPO_ITEM_START____{\"type\":\"repo\",\"stargazerCount\":39,\"repo\":\"make-github-pseudonymous-again/awesome-qr-code\"}____TRACK_AWESOME_REPO_ITEM_END--> - A type of matrix barcode that can be used to store and share a small amount of information.</li>","updatedAt":"2022-02-14T15:44:27.000Z"},{"awesomeListRepo":"sindresorhus/awesome","categoryHTML":"<h2>Related</h2>","itemHTML":"<li><a href=\"https://awesome.digitalbunker.dev\">Awesome Viewer</a> - A visualizer for all of the above Awesome lists.</li>","updatedAt":"2022-02-14T15:44:27.000Z"},{"awesomeListRepo":"fffaraz/awesome-cpp","categoryHTML":"<h2>Graphics</h2>","itemHTML":"<li><a href=\"https://github.com/google/skia\">Skia</a><a data-role=\"trackawesomelist-badge\" href=\"https://github.com/google/skia\" style=\"text-decoration:none;top: -2px;position: relative;margin-left:4px;margin-right:4px;font-weight:400;\"><span style=\"color: #fff;font-size: 11px;font-family: Verdana, Geneva, DejaVu Sans,sans-serif;\"><span style=\"padding:4px 4px 4px 6px;background: #555;border-top-left-radius: 4px;border-bottom-left-radius: 4px;\">stars</span><span style=\"padding: 4px 6px 4px 4px;background: #007ec6;border-top-right-radius: 4px;border-bottom-right-radius: 4px;\">6.4k</span></span></a><!--TRACK_AWESOME_REPO_ITEM_START____{\"type\":\"repo\",\"stargazerCount\":6430,\"repo\":\"google/skia\"}____TRACK_AWESOME_REPO_ITEM_END--> - A complete 2D graphic library for drawing Text, Geometries, and Images. [BSD] <a href=\"https://skia.org/\">website</a></li>","updatedAt":"2022-02-14T13:39:43.000Z"},{"awesomeListRepo":"zoidbergwill/awesome-ebpf","categoryHTML":"<h2>Articles and Presentations</h2><h3>Generic eBPF Presentations and Articles</h3>","itemHTML":"<li><a href=\"https://blog.cloudflare.com/tag/ebpf/\">Cloudflare's blog posts on eBPF</a> - Different blog posts about networking use cases and low-level aspects of eBPF.</li>","updatedAt":"2022-02-14T10:35:07.000Z"},{"awesomeListRepo":"zoidbergwill/awesome-ebpf","categoryHTML":"<h2>Articles and Presentations</h2><h3>Generic eBPF Presentations and Articles</h3>","itemHTML":"<li><a href=\"https://www.brendangregg.com/ebpf.html\">Linux Extended BPF (eBPF) Tracing Tools</a> - An in-depth collection of information around examples of performance analysis tools using eBPF. Contains also a section at the end of the page about other resources.</li>","updatedAt":"2022-02-14T10:35:07.000Z"},{"awesomeListRepo":"zoidbergwill/awesome-ebpf","categoryHTML":"<h2>Projects Related to eBPF</h2>","itemHTML":"<li>\n<p><a href=\"https://cilium.io/\">Cilium</a> project (<a href=\"https://github.com/cilium/cilium\">GitHub repository</a><a data-role=\"trackawesomelist-badge\" href=\"https://github.com/cilium/cilium\" style=\"text-decoration:none;top: -2px;position: relative;margin-left:4px;margin-right:4px;font-weight:400;\"><span style=\"color: #fff;font-size: 11px;font-family: Verdana, Geneva, DejaVu Sans,sans-serif;\"><span style=\"padding:4px 4px 4px 6px;background: #555;border-top-left-radius: 4px;border-bottom-left-radius: 4px;\">stars</span><span style=\"padding: 4px 6px 4px 4px;background: #007ec6;border-top-right-radius: 4px;border-bottom-right-radius: 4px;\">12.1k</span></span></a><!--TRACK_AWESOME_REPO_ITEM_START____{\"type\":\"repo\",\"stargazerCount\":12095,\"repo\":\"cilium/cilium\"}____TRACK_AWESOME_REPO_ITEM_END-->) is a technology relying on BPF and XDP to provide \"fast in-kernel networking and security policy enforcement for containers based on eBPF programs generated on the fly\". Many presentations available (with overlap):</p>\n<ul>\n<li><a href=\"http://www.slideshare.net/ThomasGraf5/clium-container-networking-with-bpf-xdp\">Cilium: Networking &#x26; Security for Containers with BPF &#x26; XDP</a> - Also featuring a load balancer use case</li>\n<li><a href=\"http://www.slideshare.net/Docker/cilium-bpf-xdp-for-containers-66969823\">Cilium: Networking &#x26; Security for Containers with BPF &#x26; XDP</a> - <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=TnJF7ht3ZYc&#x26;list=PLkA60AVN3hh8oPas3cq2VA9xB7WazcIgs\">video</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"http://www.slideshare.net/ThomasGraf5/cilium-fast-ipv6-container-networking-with-bpf-and-xdp\">Cilium: Fast IPv6 container Networking with BPF and XDP</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"https://fosdem.org/2017/schedule/event/cilium/\">Cilium: BPF &#x26; XDP for containers</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"https://ovsorbit.benpfaff.org/\">OvS Orbit episode (#4)</a> - Interview of Thomas Graf by Ben Pfaff.</li>\n<li><a href=\"https://opensource.googleblog.com/2016/11/cilium-networking-and-security.html\">A generic introduction to Cilium</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"http://blog.ipspace.net/2016/10/fast-linux-packet-forwarding-with.html\">A podcast interviewing Thomas Graf</a> - Ivan Pepelnjak interviewing Thomas, October 2016, on eBPF, P4, XDP and Cilium.</li>\n</ul>\n</li>","updatedAt":"2022-02-14T10:35:07.000Z"},{"awesomeListRepo":"zoidbergwill/awesome-ebpf","categoryHTML":"<h2>Projects Related to eBPF</h2>","itemHTML":"<li><a href=\"https://bpftrace.org/\">bpftrace</a> - A tool for tracing with its own high-level tracing language. It is flexible enough to be envisioned as a Linux replacement for DTrace and SystemTap.\n<ul>\n<li><a href=\"https://www.brendangregg.com/BPF/bpftrace-cheat-sheet.html\">bpftrace Cheat Sheet</a> - Summary and cheat sheet for programming in bpftrace. Contains information about syntax, probe types, variables and functions.</li>\n</ul>\n</li>","updatedAt":"2022-02-14T10:35:07.000Z"},{"awesomeListRepo":"zoidbergwill/awesome-ebpf","categoryHTML":"<h2>Projects Related to eBPF</h2>","itemHTML":"<li><a href=\"https://falco.org/\">Falco</a> - A cloud-native runtime security project used as a Kubernetes threat detection engine.</li>","updatedAt":"2022-02-14T10:35:07.000Z"},{"awesomeListRepo":"zoidbergwill/awesome-ebpf","categoryHTML":"<h2>Projects Related to eBPF</h2>","itemHTML":"<li><a href=\"https://github.com/Sysinternals/SysmonForLinux\">Sysmon for Linux</a><a data-role=\"trackawesomelist-badge\" href=\"https://github.com/Sysinternals/SysmonForLinux\" style=\"text-decoration:none;top: -2px;position: relative;margin-left:4px;margin-right:4px;font-weight:400;\"><span style=\"color: #fff;font-size: 11px;font-family: Verdana, Geneva, DejaVu Sans,sans-serif;\"><span style=\"padding:4px 4px 4px 6px;background: #555;border-top-left-radius: 4px;border-bottom-left-radius: 4px;\">stars</span><span style=\"padding: 4px 6px 4px 4px;background: #007ec6;border-top-right-radius: 4px;border-bottom-right-radius: 4px;\">1.1k</span></span></a><!--TRACK_AWESOME_REPO_ITEM_START____{\"type\":\"repo\",\"stargazerCount\":1073,\"repo\":\"Sysinternals/SysmonForLinux\"}____TRACK_AWESOME_REPO_ITEM_END--> - A security monitoring tool. It depends on <a href=\"https://github.com/Sysinternals/SysinternalsEBPF\">SysinternalsEBPF</a><a data-role=\"trackawesomelist-badge\" href=\"https://github.com/Sysinternals/SysinternalsEBPF\" style=\"text-decoration:none;top: -2px;position: relative;margin-left:4px;margin-right:4px;font-weight:400;\"><span style=\"color: #fff;font-size: 11px;font-family: Verdana, Geneva, DejaVu Sans,sans-serif;\"><span style=\"padding:4px 4px 4px 6px;background: #555;border-top-left-radius: 4px;border-bottom-left-radius: 4px;\">stars</span><span style=\"padding: 4px 6px 4px 4px;background: #007ec6;border-top-right-radius: 4px;border-bottom-right-radius: 4px;\">144</span></span></a><!--TRACK_AWESOME_REPO_ITEM_START____{\"type\":\"repo\",\"stargazerCount\":144,\"repo\":\"Sysinternals/SysinternalsEBPF\"}____TRACK_AWESOME_REPO_ITEM_END-->.</li>","updatedAt":"2022-02-14T10:35:07.000Z"},{"awesomeListRepo":"zoidbergwill/awesome-ebpf","categoryHTML":"<h2>Projects Related to eBPF</h2>","itemHTML":"<li><a href=\"https://redcanary.com/blog/ebpf-for-security\">Red Canary Linux Agent</a> - Red Canary has started to incorporate eBPF to their Linux security sensor.</li>","updatedAt":"2022-02-14T10:35:07.000Z"},{"awesomeListRepo":"zoidbergwill/awesome-ebpf","categoryHTML":"<h2>Projects Related to eBPF</h2>","itemHTML":"<li><a href=\"https://github.com/aquasecurity/tracee\">Tracee</a><a data-role=\"trackawesomelist-badge\" href=\"https://github.com/aquasecurity/tracee\" style=\"text-decoration:none;top: -2px;position: relative;margin-left:4px;margin-right:4px;font-weight:400;\"><span style=\"color: #fff;font-size: 11px;font-family: Verdana, Geneva, DejaVu Sans,sans-serif;\"><span style=\"padding:4px 4px 4px 6px;background: #555;border-top-left-radius: 4px;border-bottom-left-radius: 4px;\">stars</span><span style=\"padding: 4px 6px 4px 4px;background: #007ec6;border-top-right-radius: 4px;border-bottom-right-radius: 4px;\">1.9k</span></span></a><!--TRACK_AWESOME_REPO_ITEM_START____{\"type\":\"repo\",\"stargazerCount\":1897,\"repo\":\"aquasecurity/tracee\"}____TRACK_AWESOME_REPO_ITEM_END--> - A runtime security and forensics tool for Linux which uses eBPF technology to trace the system and applications at runtime, and analyze collected events to detect suspicious behavioral patterns.</li>","updatedAt":"2022-02-14T10:35:07.000Z"},{"awesomeListRepo":"zoidbergwill/awesome-ebpf","categoryHTML":"<h2>Projects Related to eBPF</h2>","itemHTML":"<li><a href=\"https://github.com/microsoft/ebpf-for-windows\">eBPF for Windows</a><a data-role=\"trackawesomelist-badge\" href=\"https://github.com/microsoft/ebpf-for-windows\" style=\"text-decoration:none;top: -2px;position: relative;margin-left:4px;margin-right:4px;font-weight:400;\"><span style=\"color: #fff;font-size: 11px;font-family: Verdana, Geneva, DejaVu Sans,sans-serif;\"><span style=\"padding:4px 4px 4px 6px;background: #555;border-top-left-radius: 4px;border-bottom-left-radius: 4px;\">stars</span><span style=\"padding: 4px 6px 4px 4px;background: #007ec6;border-top-right-radius: 4px;border-bottom-right-radius: 4px;\">1.4k</span></span></a><!--TRACK_AWESOME_REPO_ITEM_START____{\"type\":\"repo\",\"stargazerCount\":1426,\"repo\":\"microsoft/ebpf-for-windows\"}____TRACK_AWESOME_REPO_ITEM_END--> - This project is a work-in-progress that allows using existing eBPF toolchains and APIs familiar in the Linux ecosystem to be used on top of Windows.</li>","updatedAt":"2022-02-14T10:35:07.000Z"},{"awesomeListRepo":"zoidbergwill/awesome-ebpf","categoryHTML":"<h2>Projects Related to eBPF</h2>","itemHTML":"<li><a href=\"https://github.com/redcanaryco/redcanary-ebpf-sensor\">redcanary-ebpf-sensor</a><a data-role=\"trackawesomelist-badge\" href=\"https://github.com/redcanaryco/redcanary-ebpf-sensor\" style=\"text-decoration:none;top: -2px;position: relative;margin-left:4px;margin-right:4px;font-weight:400;\"><span style=\"color: #fff;font-size: 11px;font-family: Verdana, Geneva, DejaVu Sans,sans-serif;\"><span style=\"padding:4px 4px 4px 6px;background: #555;border-top-left-radius: 4px;border-bottom-left-radius: 4px;\">stars</span><span style=\"padding: 4px 6px 4px 4px;background: #007ec6;border-top-right-radius: 4px;border-bottom-right-radius: 4px;\">41</span></span></a><!--TRACK_AWESOME_REPO_ITEM_START____{\"type\":\"repo\",\"stargazerCount\":41,\"repo\":\"redcanaryco/redcanary-ebpf-sensor\"}____TRACK_AWESOME_REPO_ITEM_END--> - A set of BPF programs that gather security relevant event data from the Linux kernel. The BPF programs are combined into a single ELF file from which individual probes can be selectively loaded, depending on the running operating system and kernel version.</li>","updatedAt":"2022-02-14T10:35:07.000Z"},{"awesomeListRepo":"zoidbergwill/awesome-ebpf","categoryHTML":"<h2>Projects Related to eBPF</h2>","itemHTML":"<li><a href=\"https://github.com/linux-lock/bpflock\">bpflock - Lock Linux machines</a><a data-role=\"trackawesomelist-badge\" href=\"https://github.com/linux-lock/bpflock\" style=\"text-decoration:none;top: -2px;position: relative;margin-left:4px;margin-right:4px;font-weight:400;\"><span style=\"color: #fff;font-size: 11px;font-family: Verdana, Geneva, DejaVu Sans,sans-serif;\"><span style=\"padding:4px 4px 4px 6px;background: #555;border-top-left-radius: 4px;border-bottom-left-radius: 4px;\">stars</span><span style=\"padding: 4px 6px 4px 4px;background: #007ec6;border-top-right-radius: 4px;border-bottom-right-radius: 4px;\">62</span></span></a><!--TRACK_AWESOME_REPO_ITEM_START____{\"type\":\"repo\",\"stargazerCount\":62,\"repo\":\"linux-lock/bpflock\"}____TRACK_AWESOME_REPO_ITEM_END--> - An eBPF driven security tool for locking and auditing Linux machines.</li>","updatedAt":"2022-02-14T10:35:07.000Z"},{"awesomeListRepo":"zoidbergwill/awesome-ebpf","categoryHTML":"<h1>eBPF in Security</h1>","itemHTML":"<li><a href=\"https://embracethered.com/blog/tags/ebpf\">Embrace The Red: Offensive BPF!</a> - A series of posts around the introduction into BPF with a focus to an offensive setting, and also how its misuse can be detected. Posts include discussions on the rootkit capabilities of eBPF, or on which tracing type is needed for different use cases.</li>","updatedAt":"2022-02-14T10:35:07.000Z"},{"awesomeListRepo":"zoidbergwill/awesome-ebpf","categoryHTML":"<h1>eBPF in Security</h1>","itemHTML":"<li><a href=\"https://djalal.opendz.org/post/ebpf-block-linux-fileless-payload-execution-with-bpf-lsm/\">eBPF: Block Linux Fileless Payload \"Malware\" Execution with BPF LSM</a> - Blog post about how BPF can help detection and blocking fileless malware.</li>","updatedAt":"2022-02-14T10:35:07.000Z"},{"awesomeListRepo":"zoidbergwill/awesome-ebpf","categoryHTML":"<h1>eBPF in Security</h1>","itemHTML":"<li><a href=\"https://www.blackhat.com/us-21/briefings/schedule/#with-friends-like-ebpf-who-needs-enemies-23619\">Blackhat 2021: With Friends Like eBPF, Who Needs Enemies?</a> - Talk about an eBPF rootkit and how the capabilities of eBPF could be abused. The rootkit was also the object of a talk at Defcon, <a href=\"https://defcon.org/html/defcon-29/dc-29-speakers.html#fournier\">eBPF, I thought we were friends !</a>.</li>","updatedAt":"2022-02-14T10:35:07.000Z"},{"awesomeListRepo":"zoidbergwill/awesome-ebpf","categoryHTML":"<h1>eBPF in Security</h1>","itemHTML":"<li><a href=\"https://github.com/Gui774ume/ebpfkit\">ebpfkit</a><a data-role=\"trackawesomelist-badge\" href=\"https://github.com/Gui774ume/ebpfkit\" style=\"text-decoration:none;top: -2px;position: relative;margin-left:4px;margin-right:4px;font-weight:400;\"><span style=\"color: #fff;font-size: 11px;font-family: Verdana, Geneva, DejaVu Sans,sans-serif;\"><span style=\"padding:4px 4px 4px 6px;background: #555;border-top-left-radius: 4px;border-bottom-left-radius: 4px;\">stars</span><span style=\"padding: 4px 6px 